ON THE EARLIER MIT VERSIONS
---------------------------

Studens was published under the MIT licence from 2026-09-09 until 2026-09-19.
That grant cannot be withdrawn: anyone who received a copy during that period
keeps an MIT licence to THAT copy, for good. This file does not pretend
otherwise, and it is not trying to.

Everything from 2026-09-19 onward is under the AGPL above.

The whole history is one author's work, so there was nobody to ask: `git
shortlog -sne --all` lists a single contributor, under two addresses that are
both his.

WHY IT CHANGED, in one line, with the long version in docs/requirements.md
section 7 under OPEN-18: MIT was chosen over AGPL on 2026-09-09 in exchange for
the lowest possible barrier to outside contributors, and that exchange did not
pay. There are no outside contributors 112 commits in, and the cost accepted at
the time, that anyone may run a derivative commercially without contributing
anything back, turned out to be the one cost the author was not willing to
carry.

What the AGPL changes in practice: someone running a modified Studens as a
public service has to publish their modifications. Reading the code, learning
from it, forking it and running it for students remain exactly as free as they
were.
